            'note' => 'Instead of storing all forward activations in VRAM for backward pass, gradient checkpointing discards intermediate activations and recomputes them on-the-fly during the backward pass. Reduces activation memory from $O(N)$ to $O(\\sqrt{N})$ at cost of ~20-30% extra compute time.',
