            'note' => 'Namespaces provide isolation: determine what a process can see (own PID tree, network interfaces, mount points). Cgroups provide resource accounting and limitation: determine what a process can use (CPU shares, memory limits, I/O bandwidth). Containers are isolated Linux processes, not VMs.',
