            'note' => 'Docker CLI calls containerd daemon via gRPC. Containerd pulls layers, sets up overlayfs rootfs. Spawns `runc` (OCI runtime). `runc` calls `clone` system call with namespace flags, mounts cgroups, calls `pivot_root` to change root filesystem, drops capabilities, and calls `execve` to start process.',
        ],
        [
            'text' => 'Explain the Linux kernel Completely Fair Scheduler (CFS) bandwidth control and its interaction with Kubernetes CPU limits. How do CFS quota periods (100ms) and millicores cause CPU throttling even when overall node CPU is at 20%?',
            'category' => 'technical',
            'duration_seconds' => 180,
            'note' => 'Kubernetes CPU limit `500m` translates to CFS quota of 50ms per 100ms CFS period (`cpu.cfs_quota_us / cpu.cfs_period_us`). A multi-threaded process bursting across multiple CPU cores exhausts its 50ms quota in the first 10ms of the period, and is throttled by the OS kernel for the remaining 90ms!',
